\par\par \b \uc2 Malta's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Cuts Rates To 4.0% On Eve Of Euro Entry   \b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2007\par 12:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 The  \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Malta\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its central \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate to 4.0% Friday, just ahead of the island nation's entry into the euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union.   \par \par \uc2 The rate cut, from 4.25%, completes the process of convergence of official interest rates in Malta with those of the euro area, Governor Michael Bonello said.   \par \par \uc2 Malta, along with Cyprus, will join the European Monetary Union Jan. 1.   \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main refinancing rate is 4.0%.   \par \par \uc2 The Monetary Policy Advisory Council of the  \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Malta\uc2  will be dissolved after Friday's meeting.   \par \par \uc2 The council also noted that Malta's economic growth continued to be strong while adding that inflation has accelerated on the back of higher food and oil prices. It also urged that fiscal policy be used to anchor macroeconomic stability.   \par \par \uc2 Malta faces general elections next year.   \par \par \uc2 -By Christopher Emsden, Dow Jones Newswires; +39-02-58-21-99-05; chris.emsden@dowjones.com [ 28-12-07 1151GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071228e3cs000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
