\par\par \b \uc2  Malta cuts key interest rate 40 basis points. \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 13:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  VALLETTA, March 30 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Malta Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a reduction in its central \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by 40 basis points to 4.95 percent from 5.35 percent. \par \par \uc2  The decision, taken at a meeting of the bank's monetary policy council, follows a similar move on January 21 when the central \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate was cut by 10 basis points. \par \par \uc2  "The council will continue to monitor domestic and foreign economic and financial developments closely. It will continue to pursue a monetary policy based on maintaining a fixed exchange rate for the Maltese lira and stands ready to adjust official interest rates as necessary" the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Last December the council had decided not to touch interest rates, just weeks after Finance Minister John Dalli had said in the budget speech that a reducation in rates would serve as a stimulus to the productive sector. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's discount rate has remained untouched at 5.5 percent since 1994. The average weighted lending rate of the deposit money banks is 8.2 percent. Inflation stands at 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The exchange rate of the Maltese lira (pound) is calculated on the basis of a basket or \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  formed of the euro, the US dollar and sterling. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv3u06zxv\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\cl